      "id": "1ak30s9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to Vice President"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Vice President holds the second-highest constitutional office in the country, modeled after the American Vice President.",
        "The Electoral College consists of both elected and nominated members of both Houses of Parliament (Lok Sabha and Rajya Sabha).",
        "Members of State Legislative Assemblies do not participate in the election of the Vice President.",
        "To be eligible, a candidate must be a citizen of India, at least 35 years old, and qualified for election as a member of the Rajya Sabha.",
        "The Vice President serves as the ex-officio Chairman of the Rajya Sabha and acts as President during a vacancy for a maximum period of six months.",
        "A resolution for removal must be initiated only in the Rajya Sabha and passed by an effective majority, followed by agreement in the Lok Sabha."
      ],
      "id": "5oo8xpl"
    },
