    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Unlike the Presidential election, nominated members of Parliament CAN vote in the Vice President's election.",
        "State Legislative Assemblies (MLAs) have NO role in the election or removal of the Vice President.",
        "The candidate must be qualified for election as a member of the Rajya Sabha (NOT Lok Sabha).",
        "The Constitution does not mention any specific grounds for the removal of the Vice President."
      ],
